      "content": "\"Dear Miller family, \n\nRobert's condition has taken a significant turn for the worse over the past 48 hours. He is experiencing shallow breathing, decreased urine output, and low oxygen saturation despite supplemental oxygen. Unfortunately, he is not responding to verbal stimuli and has visible mottling on his lower extremities. \n\nAs we continue to care for Robert, we are reminded of the importance of compassion and love during this difficult time. Our team is committed to providing the best possible care, and we are grateful for the opportunity to support you and your loved one. We will continue to provide updates and answer any questions you may have.\n\nPlease know that you are not alone, and we are here to support you every step of the way.\n\nSincerely, [Your Name]\"\n\nThis version still conveys the clinical reality, but frames the situation in a way that emphasizes compassion, love, and support. The language is more uplifting, using words like \"reminded,\" \"grateful,\" and \"opportunity\" to create a more positive tone. The sentiment score should be higher, but still accurate and honest.",
